    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Better Home & Finance is building operational resilience despite a difficult mortgage backdrop, driven by accelerating home equity line of credit (HELOC) originations and deepening digital partnerships with fintech platforms. Its Tinman AI lending engine is shifting the business toward partner-driven, technology-enabled origination channels, reducing dependence on traditional purchase mortgages and broadening its revenue levers.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is guiding toward adjusted EBITDA breakeven by the end of the third quarter of 2026, supported by cost structure improvements and scaling of the AI lending platform. The strategic emphasis on fintech alliances and the HELOC segment has garnered several analyst upgrades and a consensus Moderate Buy rating, though a recent contrarian downgrade to Strong Sell injects some caution around the durability of the turnaround.",
